"""P56 handover lane: a removed member keeps only their own unhanded work (D37 ⑤).

Replaces D33's interim rule (removed members with open work kept the whole project
visible until the owner completed the removal):
- removal ends the project audience at once, so every existing project read
  (projects RLS, planning, receipts, run context) denies the person by itself;
- the server opens a per-transaction lane (`pdos.handover_lane`) only after
  `open_handover_lane` confirms an own open task, commitment or external wait, and the
  projects policy re-checks that through `project_handover_lane` on every row;
- once nothing is left, `settle_project_handover` completes the removal by the same
  deterministic rule whoever closed the last item (P56-2).

Written as placeholder s0_0873; s0_0868 since the 11-09 integration (after s0_0867;
none of s0_0862-s0_0867 touches the checked objects). Upgrade asserts the five replaced objects are exactly the s0_0859 /
s0_0790 / source_object_audience texts this was written against.
"""

